\references{
----------
Zhu, Y., Xu, Y., Yu, F., Liu, Q., Wu, S. & Wang, L. (2020) "Deep Graph
Contrastive Representation Learning", *ICML Workshop on Graph
Representation Learning and Beyond*, arXiv:2006.04131. The abstract
and Sec. 1 (a node-level contrastive objective; two views generated by
corruption at both the topology and attribute levels -- removing edges
and masking features -- to give diverse node contexts; the criticism
that DGI\'s local-global MI maximisation depends on the readout; the
theoretical connection to mutual information and the triplet loss; and
that the unsupervised method surpasses supervised counterparts on
transductive tasks). Sec. 3 (the pairwise objective with positive,
inter-view negative and intra-view negative terms, and the symmetric
average over the two views).

Velickovic, P., Fedus, W., Hamilton, W. L., Lio, P., Bengio, Y. &
Hjelm, R. D. (2019) "Deep Graph Infomax", *ICLR 2019*,
arXiv:1809.10341. The local-global objective GRACE argues against.

Hjelm, R. D., Fedorov, A., Lavoie-Marchildon, S., Grewal, K.,
Bachman, P., Trischler, A. & Bengio, Y. (2019) "Learning deep
representations by mutual information estimation and maximization",
*ICLR 2019*, arXiv:1808.06670. Deep InfoMAX; implemented in
